just one point:  {remi zdani} is not a legal tanru, since {remi} isn't a
brivla.  BUT, {le remi zdani} is (or at least might be) a legal
construction (I'm not positive about the {re}, I'll just talk about {le mi
zdani}).  This is not a tanru, but LE KOhA selbri is a legitimate way of
showing association:  {le mi zdani} == {le zdani pe mi} == The house
restrictively associated with me/us.

